Z||000005||mrfixit58||11-15-2001||05:03 PM||||What's critical about the power steering rack is it has to be a front steer rack. Most power rack are located behind the front wheels and are therefore a rear steer. The Mecurer (sp?) XR4Ti is a front steer and -- from what I hear -- is almost a direct bolt-in. I believe Rodney Dickman bought a car with one installed. There has also been a recent thread where someone was removing one from his car. Do a search and look it up (ignore the senseless flaming). You may be able to find out a few more details.<P>Good Luck,<BR><P>------------------<BR>Roy  :D <BR>Just another stock Blue 87 GT   <BR>Suncoast Fieros<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pennocksize.JPG">        <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif"> ||||reg||4
Z||000006||rockcrawl||11-15-2001||06:24 PM||||I had some pictures of a Chevette power rack fitted to a Fiero, but I cannot find them. It required that the mouning brackets be cut from the crossmember and re-welded closer together. It needed a custom shaft to connect to the column, the input shaft is not the same as the Fiero. The main problem with the Chevette rack is the length, I believe it is about 4" shorter which will cause the front tires to toe out when the suspension is compressed, also known as bumpsteer. An '84 Corvette rack fits fairly well with a little more work and the input splines match, but it is also too short. I just picked up a ZF rack from a Murkur XR4Ti. The input shaft is different (of course) and it requires quite a bit of modification to fit. It is in no way a bolt-on, not even close. The aluminum housing needs to be milled/ground/filed/sawed/hatchetized or whatever to accept the Fiero mounting bushings/straps. It may be possible to make some adapter brackets to bolt it on, I haven't had time to look at it that closely yet. The reason it was used in the aftermarket kits is the length. The rack section is exactly the same length as the Fiero rack, so it will not change the geometry at all. The Fiero tie rods will thread right on with two short pieces of M14x1.25 threaded rod. I thought that was pretty amazing. I'll be using the Merkur rack on my Rossa replica, and I'll be sure to post some pics and details when I have it mounted. ||||reg||7
Z||000007||Kasdan||11-15-2001||06:42 PM||||I did not install my rack, but i do know it was from the Merkur.  I've inspected it, and it looks like its pretty much bolt it, holes look like they line up and everything, just haev to run hoses to the pump/res.  Look for my post "The power steering nobody believes i have"  or something of that nature, i have some pics of the engine compartment.<P>------------------<BR>Tyler Morgan, 1986 GT<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/kassig2.gif">                  <BR>Aftermarket Power Steering, Rebuilt 2.8<BR>http://www.geocities.com/mtyler14/index.html||||reg||1
